<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mulayda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mulayda was fought in January 1891 in the Qassim region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-rashid">Muhammad ibn Rashid</a>, emir of Jabal Shammar, defeated an alliance of the towns of Qassim and supporters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a>. The victory made the Rashidis masters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> and ended the second Saudi state, and the Al Saud family went into exile in Kuwait.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mulayda.jpg" alt="Battle of Mulayda" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RR1886 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Mulayda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
